      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem of finding all integer values of \\( a \\) such that the polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + ax + 7 = 0 \\) has at least one integer root, we will use the Rational Root Theorem. This theorem states that any rational solution of the polynomial equation \\( P(x) = 0 \\) must be a factor of the constant term \\( 7 \\) divided by a factor of the leading coefficient (which is 1 in this case).\n\nThe factors of 7 are \\( \\pm 1 \\) and \\( \\pm 7 \\). Therefore, the possible integer roots of the polynomial are \\( \\pm 1 \\) and \\( \\pm 7 \\).\n\nWe will substitute each of these possible roots into the polynomial \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + ax + 7 \\) to find the corresponding value of \\( a \\).\n\n### Case 1: \\( x = 1 \\)\nSubstitute \\( x = 1 \\) into the polynomial:\n\\[\n1^3 + 3(1^2) + a(1) + 7 = 0\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\n1 + 3 + a + 7 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n11 + a = 0\n\\]\nSolving for \\( a \\):\n\\[\na = -11\n\\]\n\n### Case 2: \\( x = -1 \\)\nSubstitute \\( x = -1 \\) into the polynomial:\n\\[\n(-1)^3 + 3(-1)^2 + a(-1) + 7 = 0\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\n-1 + 3 - a + 7 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n9 - a = 0\n\\]\nSolving for \\( a \\):\n\\[\na = 9\n\\]\n\n### Case 3: \\( x = 7 \\)\nSubstitute \\( x = 7 \\) into the polynomial:\n\\[\n7^3 + 3(7^2) + a(7) + 7 = 0\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\n343 + 3(49) + 7a + 7 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n343 + 147 + 7a + 7 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n497 + 7a = 0\n\\]\nSolving for \\( a \\):\n\\[\n7a = -497\n\\]\n\\[\na = -71\n\\]\n\n### Case 4: \\( x = -7 \\)\nSubstitute \\( x = -7 \\) into the polynomial:\n\\[\n(-7)^3 + 3(-7)^2 + a(-7) + 7 = 0\n\\]\nSimplify the equation:\n\\[\n-343 + 3(49) - 7a + 7 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n-343 + 147 - 7a + 7 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n-149 - 7a = 0\n\\]\nSolving for \\( a \\):\n\\[\n-7a = 149\n\\]\n\\[\na = -\\frac{149}{7}\n\\]\nSince \\(-\\frac{149}{7}\\) is not an integer, it is not a valid solution.\n\nThus, the integer values of \\( a \\) that satisfy the polynomial equation \\( x^3 + 3x^2 + ax + 7 = 0 \\) having at least one integer root are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{-11, 9, -71}\n\\]",
